          "id": "ev_statute_text",
          "role": "text",
          "text": "SEC. 4. That the State Text-Book Board shall, on the first Monday\nin July, 1904, adopt a uniform series of text-books for the public\nfree schools of this State, which adoption shall continue in force\nfor a period of five years from the first day of September following.\n\nSEC. 5. The books so adopted for the several branches shall be:\n\n    Arithmetic — Milne's Standard Arithmetic, American Book Co.\n    Grammar   — Reed & Kellogg's Graded Lessons, Maynard, Merrill & Co.\n    History   — Barnes's Brief History of the United States, Am. Book Co.\n\nSEC. 6. No county, city or district board shall adopt any book for\nthe branches herein named during the life of this adoption.",
